#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:2
msgid "PyBaMM Release Policy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:4
msgid ""
"This document is the source of truth for how PyBaMM is versioned, when "
"releases happen, what counts as a breaking change, and how breaking changes "
"and deprecations are communicated. For a quick summary aimed at users, see "
"the [Versioning section of the README](https://github.com/pybamm-team/PyBaMM/"
"blob/main/README.md#versioning)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:6
msgid "At a glance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:8
msgid ""
"**Versioning:** [CalVer](https://calver.org/) in the form `YY.MM.N.P` — "
"year, month, feature release index within that month, patch level."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:9
msgid ""
"**Cadence:** We release when there's something worth releasing, with no "
"fixed schedule. Breaking changes target the first feature release of the "
"month (`YY.MM.0.0`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:10
msgid ""
"**Breaking changes:** Documented under `## Breaking changes` in [`CHANGELOG."
"md`](https://github.com/pybamm-team/PyBaMM/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md). Public "
"APIs that are removed or renamed ship a `DeprecationWarning` for at least "
"two prior feature releases first (see the Deprecation policy section for the "
"documented exceptions)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:11
msgid ""
"**Pre-announcement:** The `# [Unreleased]` section at the top of `CHANGELOG."
"md` on `main` is the canonical preview of what's about to ship."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:13
msgid "Version scheme"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:15
msgid "PyBaMM versions take the form `YY.MM.N.P`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/release.md:4
msgid "Component"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/release.md:4
msgid "Meaning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/release.md:4
msgid "Example"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/release.md:4
msgid "`YY`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/release.md:4
msgid "Two-digit year"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/release.md:4
msgid "`27`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/release.md:4
msgid "`MM`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/release.md:4
msgid "Month of release (1–12, no leading zero)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/release.md:4
msgid "`1`, `11`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/release.md:4
msgid "`N`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/release.md:4
msgid "Feature release within that month, **0-indexed** — `0` for the first"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/release.md:4
msgid "`0`, `1`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/release.md:4
msgid "`P`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/release.md:4
msgid ""
"Patch level — `0` for the feature release itself; `1`, `2`, … for patches "
"off it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/release.md:4
msgid "`0`, `1`, `2`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:24
msgid "**Worked examples:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:26
msgid "`27.1.0.0` — first feature release in January 2027."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:27
msgid "`27.1.0.1` — first patch off `27.1.0.0`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:28
msgid ""
"`27.1.1.0` — second feature release in January 2027 (only when two feature "
"releases land in the same calendar month)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:29
msgid "`27.1.1.1` — first patch off `27.1.1.0`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:31
msgid ""
"**Cutover.** The first feature release tagged after the policy lands is the "
"first to use `YY.MM.N.P`. Earlier tags (`v26.x.N`) remain in their original "
"form; we do not retroactively retag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:33
msgid "Monorepo: independent package releases"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:35
msgid ""
"PyBaMM and `pybammsolvers` live in one repository (a UV workspace under "
"`packages/`) but release **independently to PyPI**, discriminated by tag "
"namespace. See `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-11-pybamm-monorepo-design.md` "
"for the full design."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:40
msgid ""
"Each package's publish workflow fires only for its own tag namespace (the "
"pre-monorepo `github.repository` guard no longer distinguishes them)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:42
msgid "`pybammsolvers` releases use the `pybammsolvers-v*` namespace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:43
msgid ""
"**Legacy solver tags** (`v0.8.0`, `v0.8.1`, `v0.8.2`) carried over from the "
"standalone `pybammsolvers` repo are **not** part of PyBaMM's release history "
"and must not drive PyBaMM's computed version. They are either dropped or re-"
"tagged under `pybammsolvers-v*` during the migration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:47
msgid ""
"The migration was integrated with a **merge commit (not a squash)** so the "
"full commit history of both packages is preserved; PyBaMM's existing commit "
"SHAs are unchanged (no history rewrite)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:51
msgid "Release cadence"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:53
msgid ""
"We release when there's a meaningful body of work to ship. No fixed monthly "
"or quarterly schedule."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:54
msgid ""
"Patch releases are cut from the corresponding feature release branch as "
"fixes warrant."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:55
msgid ""
"Breaking changes target the **first feature release of the month** (`YY."
"MM.0.0`). Subsequent feature releases in the same month (`YY.MM.1.0`, `YY."
"MM.2.0`, …) should not contain breaking changes unless absolutely required. "
"Exceptions must be justified in the PR description and in the `## Breaking "
"changes` changelog entry, alongside the standard deprecation note."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:57
msgid "What counts as a breaking change"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:59
msgid "A change is **breaking** if it does any of the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:61
msgid "Removes or renames a public Python API."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:62
msgid ""
"Changes the signature, defaults, or return type of a public function in a "
"way existing user code would notice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:63
msgid ""
"Changes the **default** model, solver, or option such that an unchanged user "
"script produces materially different numerical output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:64
msgid ""
"Drops support for a previously-supported Python version, OS, or core "
"dependency major version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:65
msgid ""
"Changes the on-disk format of saved models or solutions without a backward-"
"compatible reader."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:67
msgid "A change is **not** breaking if it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:69
msgid "Adds new optional kwargs to existing public functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:70
msgid ""
"Adds new submodels, solvers, or options that opt-in via explicit "
"configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:71
msgid "Improves performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:72
msgid "Fixes a bug (corrects behaviour that was previously wrong)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:73
msgid ""
"Changes numerical output of a *non-default* model or solver. Algorithmic "
"improvements under the same name and same defaults are not breaking, even if "
"outputs shift."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:75
msgid "\"Public API\" defined"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:77
msgid ""
"**Public API = anything documented at [docs.pybamm.org](https://docs.pybamm."
"org).**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:79
msgid ""
"If a class, function, or method appears in the rendered API reference, it is "
"in PyBaMM's public contract. Anything else — internal modules, leading-"
"underscore names, undocumented helpers — is private and may change between "
"any two releases without a `## Breaking changes` entry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:81
msgid ""
"The rendered docs build is the auditable source of truth. A PR reviewer can "
"answer \"is this public?\" by checking whether the symbol is reachable from "
"the API reference index."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:83
msgid "Deprecation policy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:85
msgid ""
"Removing or renaming a public API must ship a `DeprecationWarning` in at "
"least **two prior feature releases** before the removal release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:87
msgid "The deprecation lands with a `## Deprecated` entry in the changelog."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:88
msgid ""
"The eventual removal lands with a `## Breaking changes` entry that "
"references the original deprecation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:90
msgid ""
"**Exceptions.** The two-release floor may be skipped only when one of the "
"following applies. Each exception must be justified in the PR description "
"*and* in the `## Breaking changes` changelog entry:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:92
msgid ""
"(a) The API is fundamentally unsafe or broken — keeping it around for two "
"releases would cause harm."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:93
msgid ""
"(b) The API was never advertised in the docs — it was reachable but not part "
"of the public contract."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:94
msgid ""
"(c) Deprecation is technically impossible — for example, removing a required "
"positional argument, where there is no behaviour to warn from."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:96
msgid "Pre-announcement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:98
msgid ""
"The `# [Unreleased]` section at the top of `CHANGELOG.md` on `main` is the "
"canonical pre-announcement channel. Downstream package maintainers, users, "
"and contributors can read that section at any time to see what is about to "
"ship."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:100
msgid ""
"The following are **not** required by policy but may be chosen by "
"maintainers for exceptional breaks (e.g. removing a long-standing core "
"class, dropping a supported Python version):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:102
msgid "Release candidate (RC) tags on PyPI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:103
msgid "Pinned GitHub tracking issues."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:104
msgid "`[BREAKING]` prefix on GitHub release titles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:105
msgid "Announcements on Slack or pybamm.org."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:107
msgid "Changelog conventions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:109
msgid ""
"Within each release block (and within `# [Unreleased]`), sections appear in "
"this order, omitting any that are empty:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:111
msgid ""
"## Breaking changes\n"
"## Deprecated\n"
"## Features\n"
"## Bug fixes\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:118
msgid ""
"The ordering is **scariest first**: anyone scanning the changelog sees "
"breaks and deprecations before features."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:120
msgid "**Entry format.** Each entry is a single bullet ending in a PR link:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:122
msgid ""
"- Short imperative description of the change. ([#1234](https://github.com/"
"pybamm-team/PyBaMM/pull/1234))\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:126
msgid ""
"Use full GitHub URLs (not bare `#1234`) so the rendered markdown on docs."
"pybamm.org links correctly. `## Breaking changes` and `## Deprecated` "
"entries must include a one-line migration note describing how users adapt."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:128
msgid ""
"**Historical entries are not rewritten.** The new section ordering and the "
"new `## Deprecated` section apply from the next release block forward. "
"Existing release blocks keep whatever they currently have."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:130
msgid "Release-manager checklist"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:132
msgid ""
"The version string in the built distribution is supplied by `hatch-vcs` from "
"the VCS tag (`pyproject.toml` has `dynamic = [\"version\"]` with `version."
"source = \"vcs\"`, writing to `src/pybamm/_version.py`). The `scripts/"
"update_version.py` helper updates `CITATION.cff` and prepends a new dated "
"heading to `CHANGELOG.md`; its version-string handling is format-agnostic "
"and accepts the four-component form unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:134
msgid "Cutting a feature release"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:136
msgid ""
"A feature release is `YY.MM.N.0` — the patch component is `0`. The first "
"feature release in a given calendar month uses `N=0`; subsequent feature "
"releases in the same month use `N=1`, `N=2`, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:138
msgid ""
"Confirm `# [Unreleased]` in `CHANGELOG.md` accurately reflects what's about "
"to ship — every breaking change, deprecation, feature, and bug fix has an "
"entry with a PR link, and entries are grouped under the four sections (`## "
"Breaking changes`, `## Deprecated`, `## Features`, `## Bug fixes`) in that "
"order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:139
msgid ""
"Create and check out a release branch from `main`: `git checkout -b release/"
"vYY.MM.N.0`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:140
msgid ""
"Run `uv run python scripts/update_version.py YY.MM.N.0` to update `CITATION."
"cff` and prepend a dated heading to `CHANGELOG.md`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:141
msgid "Push the branch and open a PR to `main`. Ensure CI passes, then merge."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:142
msgid ""
"From `main` at the merge commit, create a GitHub _release_ with the tag "
"`pybamm-vYY.MM.N.0`. Copy the relevant `CHANGELOG.md` block into the release "
"description. This triggers `publish_pypi.yml` and creates the PyPI release "
"automatically. (Monorepo: PyBaMM release tags use the `pybamm-v` prefix so "
"they are distinct from `pybammsolvers-v*`; see \"Monorepo: independent "
"package releases\" above.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:143
msgid "Verify the release installs cleanly: `pip install pybamm==YY.MM.N.0`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:145
msgid "Cutting a patch release"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:147
msgid ""
"A patch release is `YY.MM.N.P` where `P >= 1`. Patches are cut from the "
"previous tag in the same feature line so the release contains only the bug "
"fixes, not unrelated changes that have landed on `main` since the feature "
"release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:149
msgid "Ensure all bug fixes are merged to `main` first via normal PRs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:150
msgid ""
"Create a new branch from the previous tag in the same feature line: `git "
"checkout -b release/vYY.MM.N.P pybamm-vYY.MM.N.{P-1}` (e.g. `release/"
"v27.1.0.1` from `pybamm-v27.1.0.0`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:151
msgid ""
"Cherry-pick the bug fixes onto the new branch, recording the original SHA "
"with `-x`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:152
msgid "git cherry-pick -x <commit-sha-from-main>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:155
msgid ""
"Run `uv run python scripts/update_version.py YY.MM.N.P` to update `CITATION."
"cff` and prepend a dated heading to `CHANGELOG.md`. Commit the result on the "
"release branch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:156
msgid ""
"Create a GitHub _release_ with the tag `pybamm-vYY.MM.N.P` from the `release/"
"vYY.MM.N.P` branch (NOT from `main`). Copy the relevant `CHANGELOG.md` block "
"into the release description. This triggers `publish_pypi.yml`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:157
msgid "Verify the release installs cleanly: `pip install pybamm==YY.MM.N.P`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:158
msgid ""
"Update the changelog on `main` separately. **Do not merge the release branch "
"back to `main`** — that would duplicate commits with new hashes. Instead:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:159
msgid ""
"git checkout main\n"
"git checkout -b update-changelog-vYY.MM.N.P\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:163
msgid ""
"Edit `CHANGELOG.md` to add the new dated `vYY.MM.N.P` block (moving the "
"entries out of `# [Unreleased]`), and update `CITATION.cff`. Open a PR to "
"`main`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:164
msgid "Delete the release branch after tagging — it is no longer needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:166
msgid "Cutting a `pybammsolvers` release"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:168
msgid ""
"`pybammsolvers` releases independently of PyBaMM. **`packages/pybammsolvers/"
"src/pybammsolvers/version.py` is the single source of truth for its "
"published version**, *not* the release tag — the `pybammsolvers-v*` tag "
"namespace only routes the workflow. The version is a static string (dynamic "
"VCS versioning is avoided because it would force a build during dependency "
"resolution, which build-tool-less resolvers like Dependabot cannot do); the "
"`sync-pybammsolvers-version` pre-commit hook mirrors `version.py` into the "
"two static copies — `pyproject.toml` (`[project] version`, which stamps the "
"built distribution) and `vcpkg.json` (`version-string`) — so a bump touches "
"only one file. Keep the tag and `version.py` in lockstep, or the wrong "
"version ships."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:170
msgid ""
"Bump `__version__` in `packages/pybammsolvers/src/pybammsolvers/version.py` "
"(the pre-commit hook mirrors it into `pyproject.toml` and `vcpkg.json`) and "
"record the change in `CHANGELOG.md`. Open a PR to `main`, ensure CI passes, "
"then merge."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:171
msgid ""
"From `main` at the merge commit, create a GitHub _release_ with the tag "
"`pybammsolvers-vX.Y.Z`, where `X.Y.Z` **exactly matches** the new `version."
"py` value. This triggers `release_solvers.yml`, which builds wheels + sdist "
"and publishes to PyPI. The `check_version` job in that workflow fails the "
"release if the tag, `version.py`, or the `pyproject.toml`/`vcpkg.json` "
"mirrors disagree; PyPI separately rejects a re-upload of an already-"
"published version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:172
msgid ""
"Verify the release installs cleanly: `pip install pybammsolvers==X.Y.Z`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:174
msgid "Conda-forge"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:176
msgid ""
"The conda-forge release flow is triggered automatically after a stable PyPI "
"release: the conda-forge bot opens a PR against [pybamm-feedstock](https://"
"github.com/conda-forge/pybamm-feedstock), which maintainers review and "
"approve."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../RELEASE.md:178
msgid ""
"When a release touches the API, console scripts, entry points, optional "
"dependencies, supported Python versions, or core project metadata, update "
"`meta.yaml` in [pybamm-feedstock](https://github.com/conda-forge/pybamm-"
"feedstock) following [the conda-forge maintainer docs](https://conda-forge."
"org/docs/maintainer/updating_pkgs/#updating-recipes) and re-render the "
"recipe. Push updates directly to the bot's automated PR where possible. "
"Manual PRs must bump the `build` number in `meta.yaml` and be opened from a "
"personal fork."
msgstr ""
